==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|lang=la|alveolus}}, a diminutive of {{term|lang=la|alveus||a tray, trough, basin}}, from {{term|lang=la|alvus||the belly, the stomach, bowels, womb, etc.}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|alveoli}}

# A small [[cavity]] or [[pit]].
# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} an anatomical structure that has the form of a hollow cavity
# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} a small air sac in the [[lung]]s, where [[oxygen]] and [[carbon dioxide]] are exchanged with the [[blood]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|air sac in lung}} [[pulmonary alveolus]]

====Derived terms====
* [[alveolar]]
* [[alveolate]]
* [[dental alveolus]] (''syn.'' [[tooth socket]])

